WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.000
-Welcome to the show.
Thank you so much for coming on.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.200
That's how you make an entrance
right there -- to dance on.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.300
I love it.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.534
I want to talk about
a bunch of things.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.868
But "If Beale Street
Could Talk" --

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:11.000
is it true that was
your first movie ever?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.734
-Yes, yes.
-Really?

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.033
Walk me through that,

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.634
'cause it kind of changed
everything for you, right?

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.767
-It did. I mean, whew, wow.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.767
Booking "Beale Street," I mean,
that was a dream come true

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.400
and, like,
the most on-time blessing

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.033
because I was broke

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.300
when I book --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.534
...booked "If Beale Street
Could Talk."

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:28.734
-Oh, really? How broke?

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.534
-Literally, they flew me out
to New York.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.367
And so, you know, when you go
to check into a hotel,

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.701
they take your card,
they put a hold on the card?

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.167
So I gave them my card
and they said,

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.834
"Okay, we're going to put
a $100 hold."

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:38.934
I said, "Ooh."

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.868
I said, "Okay,
let's pray on that.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.801
Let's -- Whew."
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.234
Wait, you're like,
"Do I have a hu--

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.334
I don't know if $100
is going to work."

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.734
-So, thankfully, thankfully,
we had it.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.868
-Wow.
-But I went up to my room

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.000
and I checked my account,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.567
and I had $114 total
in my account.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.968
So, now I only had
$14 available.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.000
-Look at this.
It's just unbelievable,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.133
the whole story.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.534
I don't even think
I've said this before.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.367
Like, I literally --
I showed up.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.667
So, that morning,
I spent the $14 on breakfast.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.501
So, when I showed up
to my chemistry read

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.534
with Barry and Stephan,
who had already been cast,

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.467
I had no money in my account.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.634
-Zero.
-No money.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.267
-Wow.
-Seriously. So I showed up --

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.734
I think it actually
affected the energy

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:24.667
that I brought into the room of
like, "I have to book this."

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter ]
Like, "if I don't book this,

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.133
I don't know
what's going to happen."

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.167
And it's funny because at some
point, Barry offered me water.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.767
He said, "Hey, Kiki, you want
some water or anything?"

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.767
I said, "No, no thank you,
I'm okay."

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.200
And he made this joke.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.100
He said, "Oh, okay, she's not
thirsty -- she's hungry.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.901
She don't need water.
She's hungry."

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:40.934
-Wow.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.567
-And I was thinking,
"Oh, Barry."

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.901
You have no idea."
-"You have no idea."

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.501
-"I am hungry." Yeah.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.100
And you got it, and you
knocked it out of the park.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.667
-Thank you.
-I mean, nominated for Oscars.

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.000
You went to --
You presented at the Oscars.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.400
-I did. Hoo!

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.067
-I mean, to go from that to that
must be mind-blowing.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.367
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.367
The entire "Beale Street"
press run experience --

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.467
I mean, one,
it was just a huge --

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:07.033
just so many dreams coming true
night after night.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.267
But Oscar night
was even more special

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:10.634
because I brought my mom.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:11.934
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.767
-See, that's exactly why
you're awesome.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.501
Did you go, uh,
after-parties with Mom, too?

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.167
-I did. We -- Oh, we had a --
Me and my mama --

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.701
My mama loves
a good party, okay?

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.400
She is a fun time.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.167
-Yeah.
-I kind of -- It's funny.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.501
I was kind of living more
vicariously through her,

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.067
because I was trying
to play it cool.

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.968
I'm just like, "Oh, it's fine.
It's my first Oscars.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:32.133
It's totally fine.
I'm cool, I'm cool."

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.534
And my mom, "Oh, my goodness!
Hi! Hello!

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:35.868
Oh, my God, let me get a selfie.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:37.501
Yes, take a picture with me.
That's my baby.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.167
That's my baby,
Kiki Layne, yes."

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.934
-She's getting
selfies and stuff?

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.834
-Yes. Yes.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.701
-Like, what -- what --
who was at the parties?

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.567
What kind of parties
did you end up going to?

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:50.834
-The Oscar parties were crazy,

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.367
'cause you'll be just
on the dance floor

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.534
having a good time,
drinking, whatever it may be.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:55.968
And then you'll turn around.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:58.767
And it's like, "Cool, that's
Beyoncé and Jay-Z. All right."

00:02:58.767 --> 00:02:59.968
-No.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.767
-"So, I'm going to keep
twirling over here."

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.067
-I don't even know if I've ever
even seen Jay-Z dance.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:07.133
-Oh, he -- he's got some moves.
-He does?

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.133
-Oh,yes. Yes, he does.
-And what is your go-to jam?

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:10.267
Just any song?

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.601
-Um, let's see.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.434
Right now, I'm asking for --

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.701
to hear "Have Mercy"
by Chloe a lot.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:17.634
That's like --

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:18.767
Love that song, right?
-Whoo!

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.701
-Yes. That's right, look,
that's right.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:26.467
Um, and then, like, a classic,
like, forever,

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.100
no matter how many years
have passed,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.133
like, classic "I have to
dance to this song" song --

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.501
"Back That Azz Up."

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:37.567
By Juvenile.
That's right.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:38.634
-Are you one of those people

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:40.434
that go to the DJ
and request songs?

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:41.601
-Absolutely.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:42.901
-Really?
-Absolutely.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:46.000
I don't care if they have a sign
that says, "No requests."

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.100
I will request a song.
-Quest?

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.100
He says no.
-Yes.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.667
-I was the DJ that night, too.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:54.701
-Oh, really?

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.767
-Oh, that's so funny.

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.267
That's so funny.
Quest as the DJ, jamming out.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.701
Right, he's a great DJ, but --
-But see, I make great requests.

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:05.901
Because, see, I think --
-I don't.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.033
-Oh. Ohh.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.200
-I have a little something

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.200
and then I'll be like,
"Questlove.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.834
Yo, Quest, play
'We Are the World.'"

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.534
I want to talk about
a couple of things.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.701
'Cause our buddies
made this movie

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.400
"Chip and Dale: Rescue Rangers."

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.834
I love Akiva Schaffer.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.100
It's a mix of animated and real.
-Yes.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.467
-And also, like, a little salute

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.701
to animation, as well.
-Yeah.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.834
-And are you "in it"
in it, or voice in it?

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.467
-So, I am "in it" in it.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:35.734
I'm a live action lead,

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:39.367
but it was funny because
our first trailer just came out.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.801
And at the end is this beautiful
list of, like, all these iconic,

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:45.000
like, great comedians,
great actors.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.968
And then there's my name.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.334
And I'm like, "Cool.

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:50.267
I didn't actually work
with any of these people."

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:51.901
-"I never met any of this cast."
-Right.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:53.067
Like, I -- I wish.

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.534
I mean, it's such
an incredible cast.

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.133
But I didn't get to work
with any of them.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.000
It was just me, by myself,
like, running around

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.734
pretending to talk
to Chip and Dale.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:01.868
-To chipmunks. Okay, good.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.267
That's acting, right?
-Right.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.934
-Andy Samberg, John Mulaney,
uh, yeah. They're the best.

00:05:05.934 --> 00:05:07.968
I want to talk about --
you made your stage debut.

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:11.400
I love that you decided to go
back to stage and theater.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.767
Is that where you got
your start?

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:14.167
That's what made you do it,
or you just go like,

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:15.400
"I love the script"?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.501
-I had been yearning to --
to be on stage again

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.868
for like a few years actually.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.033
And then when this script
came around, I mean,

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.701
Aleshea Harris,
the playwright, is such an --

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:28.734
it's such beautiful language
and storytelling.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.267
And, like, I had been yearning

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:33.467
to dig a bit deeper
into my craft,

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.334
and this script
allowed me to do that.

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:38.200
And it's been such
an incredible experience.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.234
Just being on stage
and collaborating,

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:42.801
and this very special way
that we collaborate

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.300
and tell stories on stage
has been a gift.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.634
-And there's nothing
like a live audience.

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:47.901
-Yeah. Hey.

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.300
-Yeah, exactly right.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.334
Kiki Layne, everybody.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:53.133
"On Sugarland" is running
through Sunday

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:54.801
at the New York Theatre
Workshop.

